---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact — Freighthub"
  description="Contact Freighthub Sales, Admin and Editorial: quotation enquiries, account and privacy questions, corrections, research and republication requests."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Sales · Admin · Editorial · Last reviewed 16 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Use the department that matches your question. Commercial and quotation enquiries go to Sales;
      corrections, research and republication requests go to the Editor; account, privacy and data
      requests go to Admin.
    </p>

    <div class="contact-grid">
      <section class="contact-card">
        <h2>Sales</h2>
        <p><a href="mailto:inquiry@freightgcc.com">inquiry@freightgcc.com</a></p>
        <p>Commercial enquiries, quotation requests, supplier introductions and partnership discussions.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="contact-card">
        <h2>Admin</h2>
        <p><a href="mailto:admin@freightgcc.com">admin@freightgcc.com</a></p>
        <p>Accounts, invoicing, privacy requests and data-correction requests.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="contact-card">
        <h2>Editorial</h2>
        <p><a href="mailto:martin@freightgcc.com">martin@freightgcc.com</a></p>
        <p>Corrections, factual challenges, source suggestions, research questions and republication permission.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p>
      <a class="btn-whatsapp" href="https://wa.me/8613323237275" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Contact us now
      </a>
      <span class="contact-note">WhatsApp: +86 133 2323 7275</span>
    </p>

    <h2>What we can help with</h2>
    <p>
      Sales can discuss a commercial enquiry and tell you whether a routing or supply question can be
      quoted. Editorial can point you to the page that covers a topic, explain the reasoning behind a
      judgement, and correct a factual error. Admin handles account, privacy and data requests.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We do not publish live carrier pricing.</strong> Sales can confirm whether a routing enquiry can be quoted; any rate is subject to carrier confirmation and is confirmed in writing.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot clear a shipment.</strong> We are not a customs broker.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot give legal, tax or investment advice.</strong> The pages are editorial analysis; the decisions remain yours.</li>
      <li><strong>Editorial does not accept payment for coverage.</strong> Commercial introductions are handled by Sales and disclosed as commercial.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Response times</h2>
    <p>
      Editorial aims to acknowledge within five working days. Correction reports are prioritised.
      Sales and Admin enquiries are handled separately; include the page URL, company name and the
      decision you need to make so the message reaches the right person.
    </p>

    <h2>Before you write</h2>
    <p>
      Check the <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a> and the
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>. If your question is about a specific number, include the
      page URL and the sentence. For a commercial enquiry, include the product, route, volume and
      destination; for a privacy request, use Admin rather than the editorial inbox.
    </p>

    <h2>Postal and company details</h2>
    <p>
      Freighthub is an independent editorial and freight-intelligence project. It does not publish a
      public office address or a company registration at this stage. If that changes, it will be added
      here rather than invented.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
